English Privacy Policy

LOOPORA — Privacy Policy
Last updated: November 23, 2026
App: LOOPORA (com.toprak.loopora)
Contact: info@linesofthebrain.com

LOOPORA respects your privacy. The app does not require an account and does not transmit any personal data to any server. All of your data stays strictly on your device.

1. Data Stored Locally on Your Device

To provide core step-tracking functionality, LOOPORA stores the following information only in your device's local storage:

Your daily step count and step history
Calculated distance and estimated calories burned
Your daily and weekly step goals, streaks, badges, and sprint records
Profile details you enter: weight, height, and optional age and sex
App preferences (theme, language, and notification settings)

None of this data is uploaded to remote servers, stored in the cloud, or accessible to the developer.

2. Physical Activity and Health Data (Health Connect / HealthKit)
Activity Recognition (ACTIVITY_RECOGNITION): The app uses your device's built-in step counter sensor to measure daily steps and sprint sessions.
Health Connect (Android) and HealthKit (iOS): With your explicit permission, the app only reads your step count and step history (READ_STEPS, READ_HEALTH_DATA_HISTORY). Nothing is written back to Health Connect or HealthKit.
Limited Use: Step data obtained from Health Connect or HealthKit is used solely to display your activity inside LOOPORA (daily counter, history charts, streak and badge calculations, and the home screen widget). This data never leaves your device, is never used for advertising, marketing, or profiling, and is never shared with or sold to third parties.
You can revoke activity or health permissions at any time in your device's system settings.
3. Internet Access, Third Parties, and Data Sharing

LOOPORA has no internet permission. It contains no advertising networks, analytics tools, crash reporters, or user-tracking SDKs. Your data is never shared with, transferred to, or sold to any third party.

4. Notifications

Daily reminders, goal achievements, weekly summaries, and monthly backup reminders are scheduled and generated entirely on your device (POST_NOTIFICATIONS, RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED). No server is used.

5. Backup and Restore

Backup files are created only when you explicitly request them. You control where the file is saved or shared. The app never automatically uploads backups anywhere.

6. Data Retention and Deletion

Your data remains on your device until you choose to remove it:

You can permanently delete your step history, profile, goals, and sprint records at any time from Profile → Delete all my data.
Uninstalling the app or clearing app storage in system settings removes all local data as well.
Because no copy is stored externally, no separate deletion request is required.
Step data stored in Health Connect or Apple Health belongs to the operating system and is not deleted by LOOPORA; you can manage it directly in your system health app.
7. Children's Privacy

LOOPORA is not directed at children under 13. Because the app collects and transmits no personal data at all, no data from children is collected.

8. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected by updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this page and updating the in-app privacy policy text.

